# Product access policy (single source)

`src/creopdm/product_state.py` owns product lifecycle lock (IN_WORK + not `read_only`) for **UI flags** and **API guards**.

## When adding or changing a product mutation

Anything that changes vault/product content or locks (Add, Checkout, Check In, Remove from Vault/Product, Rename, Delete product, Collect/Rebuild metadata, Revert, create folder, …):

1. **API / service** — call `ensure_product_mutable` or `ensure_product_deletable` (do not rely on hidden buttons).
2. **Toolbar / gear** — add or reuse a flag on `ProductUiCapabilities` / `product_ui_capabilities()`; templates use `{% if product_ui.show_* %}` only.
3. **`app.js`** — selection / agent / Creo visibility only. Do **not** re-check `read_only`, product `state`, or `data-allows-mutation` to hide mutation chrome.
4. **Tests** — extend `tests/unit/test_product_state.py` for the new flag; keep integration coverage in `tests/integration/test_checkout.py` (or a focused sibling) that locked products omit the control **and** the API rejects.
5. **Docs** — update the read-only / not In work rows in `docs/user-interactions.md` when UX changes (see `user-interactions.mdc`).

`pages.render()` already injects `product_ui` from role caps ∩ product. Role permissions stay in `permissions.py` / `caps_dict`; combine them only inside `product_ui_capabilities`.

## Do not

```text
# ❌ BAD — Jinja: can_add_objects and selected.allows_mutation
# ❌ BAD — syncToolbar: mutable && canCheckout / productAllowsMutation()
# ❌ BAD — new POST handler without ensure_product_mutable
# ✅ GOOD — product_ui.show_add + ensure_product_mutable in the service
```

Undo Checkout may stay available on locked products (Checkout menu + owned row). Local workspace discard/purge may stay under `show_remove` without vault/product remove.
